    {
      "@id": "skills/library/library-core/translation-manager.md#provenance-1",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "The exported GRAPH per locale",
      "prov:value": "The pipeline used to end at the rendered page: a `.po` was injected into a\ndiagram and an SVG rendered per locale, while the graph a machine consumes was\nproduced once, in the source language."
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/library/library-core/translation-manager.md#provenance-2",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "The exported GRAPH per locale",
      "prov:value": "Four rules, and the first is the owner's and is the one an implementation\nbreaks by default."
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/library/library-core/translation-manager.md#provenance-3",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "The exported GRAPH per locale",
      "prov:value": "**4. A catalogue is scoped to the asset it was extracted from.** This one was\nlearned the expensive way."
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/library/library-core/translation-manager.md#provenance-4",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "The exported GRAPH per locale",
      "prov:value": "`kg:locale:check` says nothing about how much is\ntranslated. Measured 2026-09-22: 58 of this instance's 62 `.pot` templates are\ndiagrams and **none has a `.po` in any locale**, so the exporter writes nothing\nand reports every locale saying so.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-09-22"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-09-22"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/library/library-core/translation-manager.md#provenance-5",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "proposal",
      "cat-harness:section": "The terminology glossary — `translations/<locale>/glossary.po`",
      "prov:value": "Both halves of the corpus must stamp the same meaning. They did not until issue"
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/library/library-core/translation-manager.md#provenance-6",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "687: the generator stamped the PO-derived list while the hand-authored",
      "prov:value": "The `qa_translation_*` keys are **gone**, along with the badge that read them."
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/library/library-core/translation-manager.md#provenance-7",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "687: the generator stamped the PO-derived list while the hand-authored",
      "prov:value": "**There is no include to add**:\n`_includes/translation-warning.html` is deleted, not deprecated, as is\n`_includes/language-selector.html` — `buildLanguageBar` renders the six UN\nlanguages and greys out the ones not yet translated, which the include only\npromised in a comment."
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/library/library-core/translation-manager.md#provenance-8",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "The navbar filters by locale",
      "prov:value": "Reported by the owner, 2026-09-19:\n\n> translations are still not handled right. i have english selected, but i see\n> the translated pages in LHS navbar. the `fr/` `ru/` etc. sub-dirs need to be\n> explicitly labeled as translated content in the graph and not shown in navbar\n> unless that locale is selected. (if not present, fall back to source\n> language)",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-09-19"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-09-19"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/library/library-core/translation-manager.md#provenance-9",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "proposal",
      "cat-harness:section": "1. A page is a translation because the PAGE says so",
      "prov:value": "That is\nthe *\"distinguishable by extension … a coincidence of the current layout, not a\ncontract\"* defect #263 named, moved to directory names, and it is wrong in both\ndirections: a folio with a `no/` chapter (Norwegian, or the English word) is\nsilently hidden from its own navbar, and a `pt-BR/` or `translated-fr/`\ndirectory is silently shown as source.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "#263"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/library/library-core/translation-manager.md#provenance-10",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "proposal",
      "cat-harness:section": "1. A page is a translation because the PAGE says so",
      "prov:value": "A first draft of\nPR #351 added one, with a `locale` field on `ContentDirectory` and one\n`cat-harness.json` entry per locale subtree — ten entries for five locales\nacross two subtrees.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "#351",
        "PR 351"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/library/library-core/translation-manager.md#provenance-11",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "2. `nav_exclude` is the half that JavaScript cannot do",
      "prov:value": "It cannot know which locale\nanybody chose, so a translated page left in the nav is in it **for everybody** —\nwhich is the reported bug exactly. A script can swap a nav item; it cannot\nun-render one without a flash of the wrong nav first."
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/library/library-core/translation-manager.md#provenance-12",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "Content-type-specific translation tools",
      "prov:value": "Until\n2026-10-06 this was a literal table in cat-harness, naming four content types\nowned by layers above it (bean `0r7u`).",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean 0r7u",
        "2026-10-06"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-10-06"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/library/library-core/translation-manager.md#provenance-13",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "The terminology glossary — `translations/<locale>/glossary.po`",
      "prov:value": "The file is hand-authored and has no POT — `schemas/content/translation.ts` declares\nthat slot, and `TranslationNode.potFile` is optional for exactly this. Bean\n`he0e`.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean he0e"
      ]
    },
